Changelog

0.4.2   18 November 2026
        - Add getopts library.
        - Add standard error print functions (eprint and eprintln).
        - Fix stack handling problem when importing libraries.
        - Fix Vim syntax highlighting problem.

0.4.1   15 October 2026
        - Support text styling/colouring.
        - Add custom prompts and supporting user/host functions.
        - Add Vim syntax highlighting file.
        - Start up even if no nameservers are available, and allow
          modification of the nameserver list at runtime.
        - Update tests so that the complete build is successful on
          Nix.

0.4.0   4 October 2026
        - Add `var!` form.
        - Add option for accessing the redirect body for an HTTP
          response.
        - Handle `>>` in external commands.
        - Support stringification of RPSL objects.
        - Update `ls` to capture the working directory when it is
          called.
        - Add base64-encoding/decoding functions.
        - Add `beforei` and `afteri` functions (inclusive of condition
          element).
        - Update `b<` and `b>` to produce/consume generators.
        - Update hash functions to accept more types of input.
        - Add RPSL NRTMv3 library.
        - Various bug fixes.

0.3.0   20 June 2024
        - Closures.
        - HTTP request support.
        - General network connection support.
        - `ifconfig` and `netstat`.
        - YAML encoding/decoding.
        - Libraries for RPKI, RDAP, and RPSL.
        - Aliases for commonly-used commands (e.g. `ssh`, `git`,
          `docker`).
        - Background process management (`jobs`).
        - Improved SQL type handling.
        - Various bug fixes.

0.2.0   6 March 2024
        - Byte data type and associated operations.
        - Reification (`r`).
        - `last`, for getting the result of the previous call.
        - Parallel processing (`pmap`/`pmapn`).
        - `m{type}` functions for constructing composite object types.
        - Chained accessors for composite object types.
        - Additional data in `ps` entries.
        - `ping` and `dig`, and related functions.
        - SQL database functions.

0.0.1   11 January 2023
        - Initial release.    
